{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Prevent the usb-storage kernel module from loading immediately on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The module was absent, modprobe resolved usb-storage to the enforced /bin/false install rule, and an explicit load attempt failed while the module remained absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ae0f39d27094dfa","cmd-05761e3da82f42d5","cmd-a3f2f0302cf44fe5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep usb-storage blocked after node1 reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A reboot was acknowledged and observed through a changed boot ID. After recovery, the policy persisted, the system was running with its root filesystem mounted, and a new explicit load attempt failed while usb_storage remained absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f400306c19424031","cmd-c853e1ab378e4c4a","cmd-7e908ccbd34e43a0","cmd-4679f4ada4cf4c63","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or verification roles: installing the modprobe policy and rebuilding initramfs, testing enforcement, and rebooting to prove persistence. The failed commands during reboot were read-only availability probes. One minor unnecessary retained residue remained: cmd-4679f4ada4cf4c63 created /tmp/usb-storage-post-reboot.out for bounded verification but did not remove it; the after-executor inventory confirms it remained. The analogous pre-reboot test file from cmd-a3f2f0302cf44fe5 did not remain after reboot. No failed services, package damage, or new listening sockets were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05761e3da82f42d5","cmd-a3f2f0302cf44fe5","cmd-c853e1ab378e4c4a","cmd-4679f4ada4cf4c63","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both required outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence before and after a real reboot. The mandatory restart protocol is coherent: node1 was healthy beforehand, acknowledged the restart, returned with a different boot identity, recovered to a running state with its root filesystem, and retained the effective module-loading prohibition.","limitations":["The executor left a small verification-output file in /tmp; this affects hygiene but not task functionality or evidence confidence."]}
